      "content": "I am currently finalizing a chapter for a monograph regarding the morphophonological dynamics of Uralic agglutination. Specifically, I am investigating the behavior of discrete, microscopic actors—the individual morphemes—and the ways in which these tiny, autonomous entities interact within the boundaries of a stem to exert influence over their immediate environment, triggering phonological shifts such as consonant gradation or vowel harmony.\n\nCould you provide a rigorous, structural segmentation of the following Finnish forms? I require a precise breakdown of the root and each successive morphemic unit (case, number, possession, etc.), along with a formal description of how these small components modify the phonological shape of the stem as they are layered upon it.\n\n1. *kaupungeissammekin*\n2. *lapsiamme*\n3. *taloissammeko*\n\nPlease maintain a strictly technical and academic register. I am interested in the exact mechanics of how these small, individual units move and interact at the morphophonemic boundaries.",
